#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0033-A expect=noViolation domain=LB
#note "R-4.11b PIN, LOAD-BEARING. SVPRESP is absent AND no VISIT column exists in EITHER the evaluated dataset OR the joined SV, so this arm has nothing to read planned-ness from. The `not empty(VISIT)` conjunct is FALSE on an absent column and suppresses the rule (bucket 1). REMOVE THAT CONJUNCT AND THIS FIXTURE FLOODS: `not contains(upper(VISIT), \"UNSCHEDUL\")` is TRUE on an absent column, so every populated VISITNUM not in TV would fire. VISIT is Permissible, so its absence is legitimate. WHY SV CARRIES NO VISIT HERE, which is the whole point of this fixture: an UNQUALIFIED column name RESOLVES THROUGH `Match_Datasets`. Measured 2026-09-07 - with VISIT present on SV but not on LB, this scenario REPORTED A VIOLATION: `VISIT` fell through the left join to SV.VISIT and the guard never engaged. Dropping the column from LB alone does NOT make it absent to this rule. If this scenario reports a violation, either the guard has been removed or a joined dataset has regained a VISIT column - escalate, do not rewrite the pin."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ALB | 2
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 2 | ALB | 99
---

dataset SV label="Subject Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-1015 | 2
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-1015 | 99
---

dataset TV label="Trial Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TV | 1 | SCREENING
CDISCPILOT01 | TV | 2 | BASELINE
---
